{# The #toasts fragment, patched INNER: one notification at a time, as the panel app showed
   them (centre screen, one after another). An empty text renders an empty container, which is
   how the bare pause between the last toast and the next question is expressed.

   `kind` is success / info / warning -- the panel notification methods -- which is also Bulma's
   modifier vocabulary, so `is-{{ kind }}` needs no mapping table. #}
{% if toast.text %}
<div class="toast {{ toast.kind }} notification is-{{ toast.kind }}">{{ toast.text | suits }}</div>
{% endif %}
